  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Emergency Assistance to Communities Affected by Typhoon Yagi in Viet Nam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the overall objective of saving lives and protecting populations severely affected by Typhoon Yagi while strengthening their resilience, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) will carry out cash-based interventions (CBI) for 1,240 vulnerable households, benefiting over 4,960 individuals in need, and supporting the recovery of essential infrastructure for the affected communities. The CBI will focus on post-disaster recovery in the form of multipurpose cash assistance, conditional cash for housing repairs and cash for work for infrastructure restoration. Additionally, IOM is reinforcing the health of disaster-affected populations by providing hygiene supplies to 1,200 households and delivering public health messaging in the communities. Implemented in close collaboration with the Viet Nam Disaster and Dyke Management Authority, the Migrant Health Working Group, Viet Nam Red Cross, provincial partners and the Inter-sectoral Coordination Group, this project complements existing efforts and ensure timely and effective assistance to populations in vulnerable situations.</narrative>
  </description>
